    "title": "pandas.Index.repeat — pandas 1.5.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.repeat#\n\n- \nIndex.repeat(*repeats* ,*axis=None* )[source]#\n- Repeat elements of a Index. Returns a new Index where each element of the current Index is repeated consecutively a given number of times. \n  - Parameters\n    - **repeats** int or array of ints\n    - The number of repetitions for each element. This should be a non-negative integer. Repeating 0 times will return an empty Index.\n    - **axis** None\n    - Must be `None` . Has no effect but is accepted for compatibility\nwith numpy.\n  - Returns\n    - **repeated_index** Index\n    - Newly created Index with repeated elements.\n See also \n  - `Series.repeat`\n  - Equivalent function for Series.\n  - `numpy.repeat`\n  - Similar method for `numpy.ndarray` .\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index(['a', 'b', 'c']) >>> idx Index(['a', 'b', 'c'], dtype='object') >>> idx.repeat(2) Index(['a', 'a', 'b', 'b', 'c', 'c'], dtype='object') >>> idx.repeat([1, 2, 3]) Index(['a', 'b', 'b', 'c', 'c', 'c'], dtype='object')",
    "markdown_length": 972,
